  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring a comprehensive humanitarian data-driven response for vulnerable returnees in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan continues to grapple with the consequences of four decades of conflict, entrenched poverty, climate-induced crises, and barriers to women&#x2019;s equality and participation in public life. Despite the significant reduction in active hostilities, Afghanistan remains primarily protection emergency characterized by high levels of protracted displacement and restrictions to freedom of movement. At the same time, more than 1.9 million Afghans returned to the country in 2023, including more than 524,000 from Pakistan since 15 September 2023. Many returnees are arriving in areas already facing protracted displacement.The objective of this project is to ensure the comprehensive, evidence-informed, and data-driven response for vulnerable migrants in Afghanistan through addressing humanitarian, protection and health needs of undocumented returnees.</narrative>
  </description>
